Package: pii-guard-proxy
Version: 1.0.1
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Pre-Depends: debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0
Depends: adduser, ca-certificates
Recommends: nodejs (>= 18), libnss3-tools, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-pip
Maintainer: PII Guard <pii-guard@local>
Homepage: https://localhost
Description: Local PII anonymization proxy for LLM traffic
 PII Guard Proxy is a local HTTPS-fronting proxy that detects and anonymizes
 personally identifiable information in prompts before they reach LLM services.
 .
 Detection runs on this machine — never uploaded:
   * regex pack (30+ hand-tuned patterns: email, phone, IPs, API keys,
     credit cards, passports, SSNs, NICs, etc.)
   * supplementary regex (TIME, TITLE, SEX, addresses, structured fields,
     GEOCOORD, JSON/YAML/XML/markdown)
   * GLiNER PII Small INT8 ONNX (free-form names, addresses, IDs) — opt-in
 .
 During installation you choose which mode(s) to activate:
   * Claude Code / Anthropic SDK  (sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL system-wide)
   * Any CLI / SDK                (sets HTTPS_PROXY system-wide)
   * Browser                      (Chrome/Chromium managed policy + NSS trust)
 .
 Missing runtime packages (nodejs, libnss3-tools, python3) are installed
 automatically by the postinst script, so a plain "dpkg -i" works
 end-to-end without any follow-up commands.
